WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.515
The model selection playbook.

2
00:00:01.795 --> 00:00:07.341
The table maps task types to candidates and to the check that would confirm or overturn the choice.

3
00:00:07.621 --> 00:00:16.283
“Candidates” means what to put in your eval first, based on documented features and independent evidence at the time of review, not a verdict.

4
00:00:16.563 --> 00:00:18.333
Two rules sit under the table.

5
00:00:18.613 --> 00:00:24.971
First, include at least one cheaper tier in every comparison; teams routinely discover it is good enough.

6
00:00:25.251 --> 00:00:32.888
Second, write down what would change your mind (a new release, a price change, a failure pattern) and rerun the eval when it happens.
